review-iteration para Desenvolvedores","ru":"ИИ Агенты: review-iteration для Разработчиков","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: review-iteration لل مطورين","en":"review-iteration"},"description":{"zh":"review-iteration 是一种AI智能工具，用于优化代码和提高开发效率。通过使用该工具，开发者可以更快速地完成项目","ja":"review-iteration は、AIエージェントを使用してマニュスクリプトを最適化するためのツールです。開発者はこのツールを使用して、プロジェクトをより迅速に完了することができます","ko":"review-iteration는 AI 에이전트를 사용하여 스크립트를 최적화하는 도구입니다. 개발자는 이 도구를 사용하여 프로젝트를 더 빠르게 완료할 수 있습니다","es":"La iteración de revisión es un proceso crucial en el desarrollo de Agentes de IA. Nuestros recursos te ayudarán a dominar esta habilidad","fr":"L''itération de révision est un processus essentiel dans le développement des Agents d''IA. Nos ressources vous aideront à maîtriser cette compétence","de":"Die Überprüfungs-Iteration ist ein entscheidender Prozess in der Entwicklung von KI-Agents. Unsere Ressourcen helfen Ihnen, diese Fähigkeit zu meistern","pt":"A habilidade review-iteration é uma ferramenta de IA para auxiliar na revisão de manuscritos. Ela ajuda a melhorar a qualidade do conteúdo.","ru":"Навык review-iteration - это инструмент ИИ для помощи в рецензировании рукописей. Он помогает улучшить качество контента.","ar":"المهارة review-iteration هي أداة ذكاء اصطناعي لمساعدة في مراجعة المخطوطات. تساعد على تحسين جودة المحتوى.","en":"Manuscript"},"definition":{"en":"Manuscript"},"features":{"zh":["代码优化","开发效率提高","AI智能工具","自动化测试","代码审查"],"ja":["マニュスクリプト最適化","開発効率向上","AIエージェント","自動テスト","コードレビュー"],"ko":["스크립트 최적화","개발 효율성 향상","AI 에이전트","자동 테스트","코드 리뷰"],"es":["Revisión de código de Agentes de IA","Iteración y mejora del código","Herramientas de desarrollo de Agentes de IA","Recursos para desarrolladores de Agentes de IA","Integración con frameworks de desarrollo como React y Node.js"],"fr":["Révision du code des Agents d''IA","Itération et amélioration du code","Outils de développement des Agents d''IA","Ressources pour les développeurs d''Agents d''IA","Intégration avec des frameworks de développement tels que React et Node.js"],"de":["Code-Überprüfung von KI-Agents","Iteration und Verbesserung des Codes","Entwicklungstools für KI-Agents","Ressourcen für KI-Agents-Entwickler","Integration mit Entwicklungsfameworks wie React und Node.js"],"pt":["Análise de manuscritos com precisão","Melhoria da qualidade do conteúdo","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Suporte a múltiplos formatos de arquivo","Interface de usuário intuitiva"],"ru":["Анализ рукописей с точностью","Улучшение качества контента","Интеграция с инструментами разработки","Поддержка нескольких форматов файлов","Интуитивно понятный интерфейс пользователя"],"ar":["تحليل المخطوطات بدقة","تحسين جودة المحتوى","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","دعم صيغ الملفات المتعددة","واجهة مستخدم بديهية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用 review-iteration","什么是 AI智能工具","review-iteration 替代品","review-iteration 与其他工具的比较","review-iteration 安装","review-iteration 设置指南","代码优化工具","开发效率提高工具"],"ja":["review-iteration の使い方","AIエージェントとは","review-iteration の代替","review-iteration と他のツールの比較","review-iteration のインストール","review-iteration の設定ガイド","マニュスクリプト最適化ツール","開発効率向上ツール"],"ko":["review-iteration 사용법","AI 에이전트란","review-iteration 대체","review-iteration와 다른 도구의 비교","review-iteration 설치","review-iteration 설정 가이드","스크립트 최적화 도구","개발 효율성 향상 도구"],"es":["cómo usar Agentes de IA","qué es la iteración de revisión","Agentes de IA vs herramientas de desarrollo","instalación de Agentes de IA","guía de configuración de Agentes de IA","desarrollo de Agentes de IA con Python","Agentes de IA con CLI","alternativas a Agentes de IA"],"fr":["comment utiliser les Agents d''IA","qu''est-ce que l''itération de révision","Agents d''IA vs outils de développement","installation des Agents d''IA","guide de configuration des Agents d''IA","développement des Agents d''IA avec Python","Agents d''IA avec CLI","alternatives aux Agents d''IA"],"de":["wie man KI-Agents verwendet","was ist die Überprüfungs-Iteration","KI-Agents vs Entwicklungstools","Installation von KI-Agents","Konfigurationsanleitung für KI-Agents","Entwicklung von KI-Agents mit Python","KI-Agents mit CLI","Alternativen zu KI-Agents"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia para desenvolvedores","review-iteration para manuscritos","melhorar qualidade de conteúdo","alternativas para review-iteration","guia de instalação review-iteration","como usar review-iteration em projetos"],"ru":["инструменты ии для разработчиков","review-iteration для рукописей","улучшить качество контента","альтернативы для review-iteration","руководство по установке review-iteration","как использовать review-iteration в проектах"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","review-iteration للمخطوطات","تحسين جودة المحتوى","بديل review-iteration","دليل تثبيت review-iteration","كيفية استخدام review-iteration في المشاريع"]}},"owner":"estebandegetau","repo":"Fiscal-shocks","repoPath":"estebandegetau/Fiscal-shocks","stars":1,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-25T20:19:58Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"review-iteration","description":"Read-only structured analysis of pipeline results for human review. Diagnoses failures, maps error patterns, and suggests next steps without editing any files.","bodyPreview":"# Review Iteration Skill\n\nStructured, read-only analysis of pipeline results. This fills the gap between results existing and the user understanding what happened.\n\n**Key distinction from `/log-iteration`:**\n\n- `/review-iteration` = **read and analyze** results (before deciding what to do)\n- `/log-iteration` = **write a record** (after deciding what happened)\n\nTypical workflow: `tar_make()` -> `/review-iteration` -> discuss with user -> `/log-iteration`\n\n## When to Use\n\nInvoke `/review-iteration","body":"# Review Iteration Skill\n\nStructured, read-only analysis of pipeline results. This fills the gap between results existing and the user understanding what happened.\n\n**Key distinction from `/log-iteration`:**\n\n- `/review-iteration` = **read and analyze** results (before deciding what to do)\n- `/log-iteration` = **write a record** (after deciding what happened)\n\nTypical workflow: `tar_make()` -> `/review-iteration` -> discuss with user -> `/log-iteration`\n\n## When to Use\n\nInvoke `/review-iteration` after a pipeline stage completes and before deciding what to change. Use when you want to understand:\n\n- Which tests or metrics pass/fail and why\n- What error patterns dominate\n- Which codebook component is most likely responsible\n- What to investigate or change next\n\n## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Ask the user\n\nAsk for two things:\n\n1. **Codebook**: Which codebook? (`c1`, `c2`, `c3`, or `c4`)\n2. **Stage**: Which stage was run? (`s1`, `s2`, or `s3`)\n\n### Step 2: Auto-gather context (read-only)\n\nCollect all relevant context without modifying anything:\n\n| Source | How |\n|--------|-----|\n| Codebook YAML | Read `prompts/c<N>_<name>.yml` |\n| Pipeline results | `Rscript -e ''library(targets); cat(jsonlite::toJSON(tar_read(<target>), auto_unbox = TRUE, digits = 4, pretty = TRUE))''` |\n| Iteration log | Read `prompts/iterations/c<N>.yml` (if exists, for comparison with previous iterations) |\n| Success criteria | Read `docs/strategy.md` and extract the relevant codebook''s target metrics |\n| Previous diagnosis | Check if `/review-iteration` was run before for this codebook+stage |\n\n**Target name mapping:**\n\n| Codebook + Stage | Target |\n|------------------|--------|\n| `c<N>` + `s1` | `c<N>_s1_results` |\n| `c<N>` + `s2` | `c<N>_s2_eval` (metrics) + `c<N>_s2_results` (raw predictions) |\n| `c<N>` + `s3` | `c<N>_s3_results` |\n\nIf `tar_read()` fails, tell the user and suggest running `tar_make(<target>)` first.\n\n### Step 3: Stage-specific analysis\n\n#### S1 Analysis (Behavioral Tests)\n\nFor each of the 4 tests (I-IV):\n\n1. **Pass/fail status** with value vs. threshold\n2. **For failures**: Show the specific inputs that failed\n   - Test I: Which chunks returned invalid JSON? Show the raw response.\n   - Test II: Which label definitions were misclassified? Show predicted vs. expected.\n   - Test III: Which examples were misclassified? Show the example text and predicted vs. expected.\n   - Test IV: Which chunk+ordering combinations changed? Show the prediction pairs.\n3. **Root cause mapping**: Which codebook component (definition, clarification, example, output_instructions) is likely responsible for each failure?\n\n#### S2 Analysis (LOOCV Evaluation)\n\n1. **Primary metrics** vs. targets (from `docs/strategy.md`)\n2. **Secondary metrics** for context\n3. **Worst-performing acts**: Which acts have the lowest recall/accuracy? List the bottom 5-10.\n4. **Error category distribution** using H&K categories:\n   - A: Retrieval augmentation errors\n   - B: Prompt construction errors\n   - C: Formatting/output errors\n   - D: Non-compliance (model ignores instructions)\n   - E: Semantics/reasoning errors (model misunderstands domain)\n   - F: Ambiguous ground truth\n5. **Confusion patterns**: For classification tasks, which label pairs are most confused?\n6. **Example deep-dives**: For the 3 worst errors, show:\n   - Act name, chunk text (truncated), predicted label, true label\n   - Model reasoning (if available in raw results)\n   - Why this is likely wrong (analysis)\n\n#### S3 Analysis (Error Analysis)\n\n1. **Test V (Exclusion Criteria)**: Which negative clarifications, when removed, cause the largest accuracy drops? Rank by impact.\n2. **Test VI (Generic Labels)**: How much does accuracy change with generic labels? High change = model relies on label names, not definitions.\n3. **Test VII (Swapped Labels)**: Does the model follow definitions or label names? Quantify.\n4. **Ablation ranking**: Which components have the largest accuracy drops when removed? Top 5.\n5. **Iteration priority**: Based on ablation + error patterns, what''s the highest-leverage change?\n\n### Step 4: Present structured diagnosis\n\nUse this format:\n\n```\n## Iteration Diagnosis: [Codebook] [Stage]\n\n### What Passed / What Failed\n\n| Test/Metric | Value | Target | Status |\n|-------------|-------|--------|--------|\n| [name] | [value] | [target] | PASS/FAIL |\n\n### Error Patterns (if applicable)\n\n- [N] errors in category [X]: [description]\n- Example: Act \"[name]\", chunk [id]: predicted [X], true [Y]\n  Model reasoning: \"[quoted from raw results]\"\n  Likely cause: [analysis]\n\n### Comparison with Previous Iteration (if applicable)\n\n| Metric | Previous | Current | Change |\n|--------|----------|---------|--------|\n| [name] | [value] | [value] | +/-[delta] |\n\n### Root Cause Hypothesis\n\n[One sentence: what codebook component is most likely responsible for the dominant failure pattern]\n\n### What I''d Investigate Next\n\n1. [Ranked suggestion with rationale]\n2. [Ranked suggestion with rationale]\n3. [Ranked suggestion with rationale]\n\n### Questions for You\n\n- [Ambiguities requiring user domain judgment]\n- [Design choices where multiple valid options exist]\n```\n\n### Step 5: Stop\n\nDo NOT propose code changes, edit files, or modify the codebook. This skill is strictly read-only analysis.\n\nEnd with: \"To iterate on the codebook, you can edit it directly or start a `codebook-developer` session. When ready to record this iteration, run `/log-iteration`.\"\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T08:44:05.986Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Analysis Agents needing structured pipeline result analysis and user discussion facilitation.","zh":"适合需要结构化管道结果分析和用户讨论促进的AI分析代理。","ja":"構造化されたパイプライン結果分析とユーザーのディスカッション促進が必要なAI分析エージェントに適しています。","ko":"구조화된 파이프라인 결과 분석 및 사용자 토론 촉진이 필요한 AI 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de inteligencia artificial que necesitan un análisis de resultados de tuberías estructurados y facilitación de discusiones de usuarios.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse d''intelligence artificielle nécessitant une analyse de résultats de pipeline structurée et une facilitation de discussion utilisateur.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Analyseagenten, die eine strukturierte Analyse der Pipeline-Ergebnisse und eine Benutzerdiskussionsfacilitation benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de IA que necessitam de análise de resultados de pipeline estruturada e facilitação de discussão de usuário.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа ИИ, которым требуется структурированный анализ результатов конвейера и облегчение обсуждения пользователей.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء تحليل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى تحليل نتائج трубة منظم و تسهيل مناقشة المستخدم."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to read and analyze pipeline results using tar_make() and /review-iteration, providing comprehensive content analysis and facilitating user discussions through protocols like log-iteration.","zh":"赋予代理读取和分析管道结果的能力，使用tar_make()和/review-iteration，提供全面内容分析，并通过类似log-iteration的协议促进用户讨论。","ja":"エージェントがtar_make()と/review-iterationを使用してパイプライン結果を読み取って分析する機能を提供し、包括的なコンテンツ分析を行い、log-iterationなどのプロトコルを介してユーザーのディスカッションを促進します。","ko":"에이전트가 tar_make()와 /review-iteration을 사용하여 파이프라인 결과를 읽고 분석할 수 있는 기능을 제공하며, 포괄적인 콘텐츠 분석을 수행하며, log-iteration과 같은 프로토콜을 통해 사용자 토론을 촉진합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a leer y analizar los resultados de la tubería utilizando tar_make() y /review-iteration, proporcionando un análisis de contenido integral y facilitando las discusiones de los usuarios a través de protocolos como log-iteration.","fr":"Permet aux agents de lire et d''analyser les résultats du pipeline à l''aide de tar_make() et /review-iteration, fournissant une analyse de contenu complète et facilitant les discussions des utilisateurs via des protocoles tels que log-iteration.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Pipeline-Ergebnisse mithilfe von tar_make() und /review-iteration zu lesen und zu analysieren, um eine umfassende Inhaltsanalyse bereitzustellen und Benutzerdiskussionen durch Protokolle wie log-iteration zu erleichtern.","pt":"Habilita agentes a ler e analisar resultados de pipeline usando tar_make() e /review-iteration, fornecendo análise de conteúdo abrangente e facilitando discussões de usuário por meio de protocolos como log-iteration.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью читать и анализировать результаты конвейера с помощью tar_make() и /review-iteration, предоставляя всесторонний анализ содержания и облегчая обсуждения пользователей посредством протоколов, таких как log-iteration.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية قراءة وتحليل نتائج трубة باستخدام tar_make() و /review-iteration، و يوفر تحليل محتوى شامل ويسهل مناقشات المستخدم من خلال بروتوكولات مثل log-iteration."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing manuscript pipeline results","Facilitating user discussions on pipeline outcomes","Structuring read-only analysis of results before logging iterations"],"zh":["分析手稿管道结果","促进用户对管道结果的讨论","结构化只读分析结果在记录迭代之前"],"ja":["原稿パイプライン結果の分析","パイプライン結果に関するユーザーのディスカッションの促進","結果の読み取り専用分析の構造化（イテレーションの記録前に）"],"ko":["원고 파이프라인 결과 분석","파이프라인 결과에 대한 사용자 토론 촉진","결과에 대한 읽기 전용 분석 구조화(반복 기록 이전에)"],"es":["Análisis de resultados de tuberías de manuscritos","Facilitación de discusiones de usuarios sobre los resultados de la tubería","Estructuración del análisis de solo lectura de resultados antes de registrar iteraciones"],"fr":["Analyse des résultats de pipeline de manuscrits","Facilitation des discussions des utilisateurs sur les résultats du pipeline","Structuration de l''analyse en lecture seule des résultats avant d''enregistrer les itérations"],"de":["Analyse der Ergebnisse von Manuskript-Pipelines","Erleichterung von Benutzerdiskussionen über Pipeline-Ergebnisse","Strukturierung der schreibgeschützten Analyse von Ergebnissen vor der Aufzeichnung von Iterationen"],"pt":["Analisar resultados de pipeline de manuscritos","Facilitar discussões de usuário sobre resultados de pipeline","Estruturar análise somente leitura de resultados antes de registrar iterações"],"ru":["Анализировать результаты конвейера рукописей","Облегчать обсуждения пользователей о результатах конвейера","Структурировать анализ только для чтения ре