oring","ar":"أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي: moonbit-refactoring","en":"moonbit-refactoring"},"description":{"zh":"moonbit-refactoring是shiguredo/http11-rs的Rust端口，用于提高代码质量和性能","ja":"moonbit-refactoringはshiguredo/http11-rsのRust移植で、コード品質とパフォーマンスを向上させます","ko":"moonbit-refactoring은 shiguredo/http11-rs의 러스트 포팅으로 코드 품질과 성능을 개선합니다","es":"Moonbit-refactoring es una herramienta de inteligencia artificial que permite refactorizar código de manera eficiente, basada en shiguredo/http11-rs","fr":"Moonbit-refactoring est un outil d''intelligence artificielle qui permet de refactoriser du code de manière efficace, basé sur shiguredo/http11-rs","de":"Moonbit-refactoring ist ein KI-Tool, das das Refactoring von Code auf effiziente Weise ermöglicht, basierend auf shiguredo/http11-rs","pt":"O moonbit-refactoring é uma ferramenta de refatoração baseada em AI, criada a partir do port de shiguredo/http11-rs","ru":"ИИ Агент moonbit-refactoring - инструмент рефакторинга на основе ИИ, созданный на основе порта shiguredo/http11-rs","ar":"أداة moonbit-refactoring هي أداة تحسين.setCode باستخدام الذكاء الاصطناعي، تم إنشاؤها من خلال منفذ shiguredo/http11-rs","en":"port from shiguredo/http11-rs"},"definition":{"en":"port from shiguredo/http11-rs"},"features":{"zh":["基于Rust语言","提高代码质量","提高代码性能","支持http11-rs协议","轻量级和高效"],"ja":["Rust言語をベースに","コード品質の向上","コードパフォーマンスの向上","http11-rsプロトコルのサポート","軽量級で高効率"],"ko":["러스트 언어를 기반으로","코드 품질 개선","코드 성능 개선","http11-rs 프로토콜 지원","경량級과 고효율"],"es":["Refactorización de código eficiente","Basado en shiguredo/http11-rs","Herramienta de inteligencia artificial","Mejora de la calidad del código","Compatibilidad con diferentes lenguajes de programación"],"fr":["Refactorisation de code efficace","Basé sur shiguredo/http11-rs","Outil d''intelligence artificielle","Amélioration de la qualité du code","Compatibilité avec différents langages de programmation"],"de":["Effizientes Refactoring von Code","Basierend auf shiguredo/http11-rs","KI-Tool","Verbesserung der Codequalität","Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen Programmiersprachen"],"pt":["Refatoração automática de código","Baseado em AI","Port de shiguredo/http11-rs","Melhoria da qualidade do código","Redução de complexidade"],"ru":["Автоматическая рефакторинга кода","На основе ИИ","Порт shiguredo/http11-rs","Улучшение качества кода","Снижение сложности"],"ar":["تحسين الكود تلقائيًا","استخدام الذكاء الاصطناعي","منفذ shiguredo/http11-rs","تحسين جودة الكود","تقليل التعقيد"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI工具","代码重构","Rust语言","http11-rs","代码质量","代码性能","moonbit-refactoring教程","moonbit-refactoring安装","AI工具比较"],"ja":["AIエージェント","コードリファクタリング","Rust言語","http11-rs","コード品質","コードパフォーマンス","moonbit-refactoringマニュアル","moonbit-refactoringインストール","AIエージェント比較"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","코드 리팩토링","러스트 언어","http11-rs","코드 품질","코드 성능","moonbit-refactoring 사용법","moonbit-refactoring 설치","AI 에이전트 비교"],"es":["herramientas de inteligencia artificial","refactorizar código","shiguredo/http11-rs","mejora de código","herramientas de desarrollo","cómo usar moonbit-refactoring","alternativas a moonbit-refactoring","moonbit-refactoring vs otros herramientas","instalación de moonbit-refactoring","guía de configuración de moonbit-refactoring"],"fr":["outils d''intelligence artificielle","refactoriser du code","shiguredo/http11-rs","amélioration de code","outils de développement","comment utiliser moonbit-refactoring","alternatives à moonbit-refactoring","moonbit-refactoring vs autres outils","installation de moonbit-refactoring","guide de configuration de moonbit-refactoring"],"de":["KI-Tools","Code refaktorisieren","shiguredo/http11-rs","Codeverbesserung","Entwicklungstools","wie man moonbit-refactoring verwendet","Alternativen zu moonbit-refactoring","moonbit-refactoring vs andere Tools","Installation von moonbit-refactoring","Konfigurationsanleitung für moonbit-refactoring"],"pt":["como usar moonbit-refactoring","o que é refatoração de código","ferramentas de AI para desenvolvedores","moonbit-refactoring vs outros ferramentas","instalar moonbit-refactoring","guia de configuração do moonbit-refactoring"],"ru":["как использовать moonbit-refactoring","что такое рефакторинга кода","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков","moonbit-refactoring vs другие инструменты","установить moonbit-refactoring","руководство по настройке moonbit-refactoring"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أداة moonbit-refactoring","ما هي تحسين الكود","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","أداة moonbit-refactoring مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت أداة moonbit-refactoring","دليل إعداد أداة moonbit-refactoring"]}},"owner":"f4ah6o","repo":"http11.mbt","repoPath":"f4ah6o/http11.mbt","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.969Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"moonbit-refactoring","description":"Refactor MoonBit code to be idiomatic: shrink public APIs, convert functions to methods, use pattern matching with views, add loop invariants, and ensure test coverage without regressions. Use when updating MoonBit packages or refactoring MoonBit APIs, modules, or tests.","bodyPreview":"# MoonBit Refactoring Skill\n\n## Intent\n- Preserve behavior and public contracts unless explicitly changed.\n- Minimize the public API to what callers require.\n- Prefer declarative style and pattern matching over incidental mutation.\n- Use view types (ArrayView/StringView/BytesView) to avoid copies.\n- Add tests and docs alongside refactors.\n\n## Workflow\n**Start broad, then refine locally:**\n\n1. **Architecture first**: Review package structure, dependencies, and API boundaries.\n2. **Inventory** pub","body":"# MoonBit Refactoring Skill\n\n## Intent\n- Preserve behavior and public contracts unless explicitly changed.\n- Minimize the public API to what callers require.\n- Prefer declarative style and pattern matching over incidental mutation.\n- Use view types (ArrayView/StringView/BytesView) to avoid copies.\n- Add tests and docs alongside refactors.\n\n## Workflow\n**Start broad, then refine locally:**\n\n1. **Architecture first**: Review package structure, dependencies, and API boundaries.\n2. **Inventory** public APIs and call sites (`moon doc`, `moon ide find-references`).\n3. **Pick one refactor theme** (API minimization, package splits, pattern matching, loop style).\n4. **Apply the smallest safe change**.\n5. **Update docs/tests** in the same patch.\n6. **Run `moon check`, then `moon test`**.\n7. **Use coverage** to target missing branches.\n\nAvoid local cleanups (renaming, pattern matching) until the high-level structure is sound.\n\n## Improve Package Architecture\n- Keep packages focused: aim for <10k lines per package.\n- Keep files manageable: aim for <2k lines per file.\n- Keep functions focused: aim for <200 lines per function.\n\n### Splitting Files\nTreat files in MoonBit as organizational units; move code freely within a package as long as each file stays focused on one concept.\n\n### Splitting Packages\nWhen spinning off package `A` into `A` and `B`:\n\n1. Create the new package and re-export temporarily:\n   ```mbt\n   // In package B\n   using @A { ... }  // re-export A''s APIs\n   ```\n   Ensure `moon check` passes before proceeding.\n\n2. Find and update all call sites:\n   ```bash\n   moon ide find-references <symbol>\n   ```\n   Replace bare `f` with `@B.f`.\n\n3. Remove the `use` statement once all call sites are updated.\n\n4. Audit and remove newly-unused `pub` APIs from both packages.\n\n### Guidelines\n- Prefer acyclic dependencies: lower-level packages should not import higher-level ones.\n- Only expose what downstream packages actually need.\n- Consider an `internal/` package for helpers that shouldn''t leak.\n\n## Minimize Public API and Modularize\n- Remove `pub` from helpers; keep only required exports.\n- Move helpers into `internal/` packages to block external imports.\n- Split large files by feature; files do not define modules in MoonBit.\n\n## Local refactoring\n\n### Convert Free Functions to Methods + Chaining\n- Move behavior onto the owning type for discoverability.\n- Use `..` for fluent, mutating chains when it reads clearly.\n\nExample:\n```mbt nocheck\n// Before\nfn reader_next(r : Reader) -> Char? { ... }\nlet ch = reader_next(r)\n\n// After\nfn Reader::next(self : Reader) -> Char? { ... }\nlet ch = r.next()\n```\n\nExample (chaining):\n```mbt nocheck\nbuf..write_string(\"#\\\\\")..write_char(ch)\n```\n\n### Prefer Explicit Qualification\n- Use `@pkg.fn` instead of `using` when clarity matters.\n- Keep call sites explicit during wide refactors.\n\nExample:\n```mbt nocheck\nlet n = @parser.parse_number(token)\n```\n\n### Simplify Enum Constructors When Type Is Known\n\nWhen the expected type is known from context, you can omit the full package path for enum constructors:\n\n- **Pattern matching**: Annotate the matched value; constructors need no path.\n- **Nested constructors**: Only the outermost needs the full path.\n- **Return values**: The return type provides context for constructors in the body.\n- **Collections**: Type-annotate the collection; elements inherit the type.\n\nExamples:\n```mbt\n// Pattern matching - annotate the value being matched\nlet tree : @pkga.Tree = ...\nmatch tree {\n  Leaf(x) => x\n  Node(left~, x, right~) => left.sum() + x + right.sum()\n}\n\n// Nested constructors - only outer needs full path\nlet x = @pkga.Tree::Node(left=Leaf(1), x=2, right=Leaf(3))\n\n// Return type provides context\nfn make_tree() -> @pkga.Tree {\n  Node(left=Leaf(1), x=2, right=Leaf(3))\n}\n\n// Collections - type annotation on the array\nlet trees : Array[@pkga.Tree] = [Leaf(1), Node(left=Leaf(2), x=3, right=Leaf(4))]\n```\n\n### Pattern Matching and Views\n- Pattern match arrays directly; the compiler inserts ArrayView implicitly.\n- Use `..` in the middle to match prefix and suffix at once.\n- Pattern match strings directly; avoid converting to `Array[Char]`.\n- `String`/`StringView` indexing yields `UInt16` code units. Use `for ch in s` for Unicode-aware iteration.\n\n#### we prefer pattern matching over small functions\n\nFor example,\n```mbt\n match gen_results.get(0) {\n   Some(value) => Iter::singleton(value)\n   None => Iter::empty()\n }\n```\nWe can pattern match directly, it is more efficient and as readable:\n```mbt\n match gen_results {\n   [value, ..] => Iter::singleton(value)\n   [] => Iter::empty()\n }\n```\nMoonBit pattern matching is pretty expressive, here are some more examples:\n```mbt\nmatch items {\n  [] => ()\n  [head, ..tail] => handle(head, tail)\n  [..prefix, mid, ..suffix] => handle_mid(prefix, mid, suffix)\n}\n```\n\n```mbt\nmatch s {\n  \"\" => ()\n  [..\"let\", ..rest] => handle_let(rest)\n  _ => ()\n}\n```\n#### Char literal matching\n\nUse char literal overloading for `Char`, `UInt16`, and `Int`; the examples below rely on it. This is handy when matching `String` indexing results (`UInt16`) against a char range.\n```mbt\ntest {\n  let a_int : Int = ''b''\n  if (a_int is ''a''..<''z'') { () } else { () }\n  let a_u16 : UInt16 = ''b''\n  if (a_u16 is ''a''..<''z'') { () } else { () }\n  let a_char : Char = ''b''\n  if (a_char is ''a''..<''z'') { () } else { () }\n}\n```\n\n#### Use Nested Patterns and `is`\n\n- Use `is` patterns inside `if`/`guard` to keep branches concise.\n\nExample:\n```mbt\nmatch token {\n  Some(Ident([..\"@\", ..rest])) if process(rest) is Some(x) => handle_at(rest)\n  Some(Ident(name)) => handle_ident(name)\n  None => ()\n}\n```\n\n#### Prefer Range Loops for Simple Indexing\n- Use `for i in start..<end { ... }`, `for i in start..<=end { ... }`, `for i in large>..small`, or `for i in large>=..small` for simple index loops.\n- Keep functional-state `for` loops for algorithms that update state.\n\nExample:\n```mbt\n// Before\nfor i = 0; i < len; {\n  items.push(fill)\n  continue i + 1\n}\n\n// After\nfor i in 0..<len {\n  items.push(fill)\n}\n```\n\n## Loop Specs (Dafny-Style Comments)\n- Add specs for functional-state loops.\n- Skip invariants for simple `for x in xs` loops.\n- Add TODO when a decreases clause is unclear (possible bug).\n\nExample:\n```mbt\nfor i = 0, acc = 0; i < xs.length(); {\n  acc = acc + xs[i]\n  i = i + 1\n} else { acc }\nwhere {\n  invariant: 0 <= i <= xs.length(),\n  reasoning: (\n    #| ... rigorous explanation ...\n    #| ...\n  )\n}\n```\n\n\n### Tests and Docs\n- Prefer black-box tests in `*_test.mbt` or `*.mbt.md`.\n- Add docstring tests with `mbt check` for public APIs.\n\nExample:\n```mbt\n///|\n/// Return the last element of a non-empty array.\n///\n/// # Example\n/// ```mbt check\n/// test {\n///   inspect(last([1, 2, 3]), content=\"3\")\n/// }\n/// ```\npub fn last(xs : Array[Int]) -> Int { ... }\n```\n\n## Coverage-Driven Refactors\n- Use coverage to target missing branches through public APIs.\n- Prefer small, focused tests over white-box checks.\n\nCommands:\n```bash\nmoon coverage analyze -- -f summary\nmoon coverage analyze -- -f caret -F path/to/file.mbt\n```\n\n## Moon IDE Commands\n\n```bash\nmoon doc \"<query>\"\nmoon ide outline <dir|file>\nmoon ide find-references <symbol>\nmoon ide peek-def <symbol>\nmoon ide rename <symbol> -new-name <new_name>\nmoon check\nmoon test\nmoon info\n```\nUse these commands for reliable refactoring.\n\nExample: spinning off `package_b` from `package_a`.\n\nTemporary import in `package_b`:\n```mbt\nusing @package_a { a, type B }\n```\n\nSteps:\n1. Use `moon ide find-references <symbol>` to find all call sites of `a` and `B`.\n2. Replace them with `@package_a.a` and `@package_a.B`.\n3. Remove the `using` statement and run `moon check`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:53:14.025Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Rust-focused AI Agents requiring advanced code refactoring and optimization capabilities, particularly with http11-rs libraries.","zh":"适用于需要高级代码重构和优化能力的 Rust 专注 AI 代理，特别是使用 http11-rs 库。","ja":"Rust に焦点を当てた AI エージェントが高度なコードのリファクタリングと最適化機能を必要とする場合、特に http11-rs ライブラリを使用する場合に適しています。","ko":"Rust에 중점을 둔 AI 에이전트가 고급 코드 리팩토링 및 최적화 기능을 필요로 하는 경우, 특히 http11-rs 라이브러리를 사용하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA enfocados en Rust que requieren capacidades de refactorización y optimización de código avanzadas, particularmente con bibliotecas http11-rs.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA axés sur Rust nécessitant des capacités de réorganisation et d''optimisation de code avancées, en particulier avec les bibliothèques http11-rs.","de":"Ideal für Rust-fokussierte KI-Agents, die erweiterte Code-Refactoring- und Optimierungsfähigkeiten benötigen, insbesondere mit http11-rs-Bibliotheken.","pt":"Ideal para AI Agents focados em Rust que requerem capacidades avançadas de refatoração e otimização de código, particularmente com bibliotecas http11-rs.","ru":"Идеально подходит для AI-агентов, ориентированных на Rust, которым требуются расширенные возможности рефакторинга и оптимизации кода, особенно с библиотеками http11-rs.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي المرتكزة على Rust والتي تتطلب قدرات متقدمة لإعادة هيكلة وتحسين التعليمات البرمجية، خاصة مع مكتبات http11-rs."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to refactor Rust codebases using declarative styles, pattern matching, and view types like ArrayView, StringView, and BytesView, while preserving public contracts and minimizing API boundaries, utilizing protocols and libraries such as shiguredo/http11-rs.","zh":"赋予代理使用声明式样式、模式匹配和视图类型（如 ArrayView、StringView 和 BytesView）重构 Rust 代码库的能力，同时保留公共契约并最小化 API 边界，利用诸如 shiguredo/http11-rs 的协议和库。","ja":"エージェントが宣言的なスタイル、パターンマッチング、ArrayView、StringView、BytesView などのビュー型を使用して Rust コードベースをリファクタリングできるようにし、公契約を保持し、API の境界を最小限に抑え、shiguredo/http11-rs などのプロトコルとライブラリを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 선언적 스타일, 패턴 매칭 및 ArrayView, StringView, BytesView 등의 뷰 유형을 사용하여 Rust 코드베이스를 리팩토링할 수 있도록 하며, 공용 계약을 유지하고 API 경계를 최소화하며, shiguredo/http11-rs 등의 프로토콜 및 라이브러리를 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes reorganizar las bases de código de Rust utilizando estilos declarativos, coincidencia de patrones y tipos de vista como ArrayView, StringView y BytesView, preservando los contratos públicos y minimizando los límites de la API, utilizando protocolos y bibliotecas como shiguredo/http11-rs.","fr":"Permet aux agents de réorganiser les bases de code Rust en utilisant des styles déclaratifs, la correspondance de modèles et des types de vue tels que ArrayView, StringView et BytesView, en préservant les contrats publics et en minimisant les limites de l''API, en utilisant des protocoles et des bibliothèques tels que shiguredo/http11-rs.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Rust-Codebasen unter Verwendung deklarativer Stile, Mustervergleichs und Ansichtstypen wie ArrayView, StringView und BytesView zu refaktorisieren, wobei öffentliche Verträge erhalten und API-Grenzen minimiert werden, unter Verwendung von Protokollen und Bibliotheken wie shiguredo/http11-rs.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a refatorar bases de código Rust usando estilos declarativos, correspondência de padrões e tipos de visualização como ArrayView, StringView e BytesView, preservando contratos públicos e minimizando os limites da API, utilizando protocolos e bibliotecas como shiguredo/http11-rs.","ru":"Позволяет агентам проводить рефакторинг кодовой базы Rust с использованием декларативных стилей, сопоставления с образцом и типов представления, таких как ArrayView, StringView и BytesView, при сохранении публичных контрактов и минимизации границ API с использованием протоколов и библиотек, таких как shiguredo/http11-rs.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من إعادة هيكلة قواعد تعليمات Rust البرمجية باستخدام الأنواع التصريحية، ومطابقة الأنماط، وأنواع العرض مثل ArrayView و StringView و BytesView، مع الحفاظ على العقود العامة وتقليل حدود واجهة برمجة التطبيقات إلى الحد الأدنى، باستخدام بروتوكولات ومكتبات مثل shiguredo/http11-rs."},"useCases":{"en":["Refactoring large Rust codebases to improve maintainability","Optimizing http11-rs implementations for better performance","Minimizing public API surfaces for enhanced security"],"zh":["重构大型 Rust 代码库以提高可维护性","优化 http11-rs 实现以获得更好的性能","最小化公共 API 表面以增强安全性"],"ja":["メンテナンス性を向上させるために大規模な Rust コードベースをリファクタリングする","パフォーマンスを向上させるために http11-rs の実装を最適化する","セキュリティを強化するために公開 API サーフェスを最小限に抑える"],"ko":["유지 보수성을 향상시키기 위해 대규모 Rust 코드베이스를 리팩토링하는 것","성능을 향상시키기 위해 http11-rs 구현을 최적화하는 것","보안을 강화하기 위해 공개 API 표면을 최소화하는 것"],"es":["Reorganizar grandes bases de código de Rust para mejorar la mantenibilidad","Optimizar implementaciones de http11-rs para un mejor rendimiento","Minimizar superficies de API públicas para mejorar la seguridad"],"fr":["Réorganiser de grandes bases de code Rust pour améliorer la maintenabilité","Optimiser les implémentations http11-rs pour de meilleures performances","Minimiser les surfaces d''API publiques pour améliorer la sécurité"],"de":["Große Rust-Codebasen neu organisieren, um die Wartbarkeit zu verbessern","http11-rs-Implementierungen optimieren, um die Leistung zu verbessern","Öffentliche API-Oberflächen minimieren, um die Sicherheit zu verbessern"],"pt":["Refatoração de grandes bases de código Rust para melhorar a capacidade de manutenção","Otimização de implementações http11-rs para melhor desempenho","Minimização de superfícies públicas de API para segurança aprimorada"],"ru":["Рефакторинг больших кодовых баз Rust для повышения сопровождаемости","Оптимизация реализаций http11-rs для повышения производительности","Минимизация публичных поверхностей API для повышения безопасности"],"ar":["إعادة هيكلة قواعد تعليمات Rust البرمجية الكبيرة لتحسين القابلية للصيانة","تحسين تطبيقات http11-rs لأداء أفضل","تقليل واجهات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات (API) العامة لتعزيز الأمان"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Rust programming language","Specific to http11-rs library and its dependencies","Needs comprehensive testing and documentation alongside refactors"],"zh":["需要 Rust 编程语言的知识","特定于 http11-rs 库及其依赖项","需要在重构过程中进行全面测试和文档化"],"ja":["Rust プログラミング言語の知識が必要","http11-rs ライブラリとその依存関係に特化","リファクタリングの際に包括的なテストとドキュメントが必要"],"ko":["Rust 프로그래밍 언어에 대한 지식이 필요","http11-rs 라이브러리及其 종속성에 특화","리팩토링 과정에서 포괄적인 테스트 및 문서화가 필요"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento del lenguaje de programación Rust","Específico de la biblioteca http11-rs y sus dependencias","Necesita pruebas y documentación exhaustivas junto con las reorganizaciones"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance du langage de programmation Rust","Spécifique à la bibliothèque http11-rs et ses dépendances","Nécessite des tests et une documentation exhaustifs aux côtés des réorganisations"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der Rust-Programmiersprache","Spezifisch für die http11-rs-Bibliothek und ihre Abhängigkeiten","Benötigt umfassende Tests und Dokumentation neben der Refaktorisierung"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento da linguagem de programação Rust","Específico para a biblioteca http11-rs e suas dependências","Requer testes abrangentes e documentação juntamente com as refatorações"],"ru":["Требует знания языка программирования Rust","Специфично для библиотеки http11-rs и её зависимостей","Требует всестороннего тестирования и документации наряду с рефакторингом"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة بلغة البرمجة Rust","مخصص لمكتبة http11-rs والتبعيات الخاصة بها","يتطلب اختبارات شاملة ووثائقًا إلى جانب عمليات إعادة الهيكلة"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"ff6b5153224058ba920ec1d07af2d974bf4b79457e8ba06ba1c4b7cc219d8975","qualityScore":49}');
